e, of the period and after, were Edmund Bannerman, younger brother of Charles, and the late Robert Hansen, known among his friends in his day as the “Hermit.” I had the pleasure of meeting this gentleman in 1893 when I was sub-editing the Gold Coast Chronicle at Accra\'  Native elites employed couriers rather than a general postal service (see above).'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1810, 'temperature': 0.2})
