l and in some instances external, from 1926 to 1948, and has been read by Western observers as a record of “efforts to form a national consciousness” (Rossi 1938: 569) and of “the institutionalization of the state” (Obermeyer 1981: 181).\'  Given the importance of tribal structures for local governance, no general postal service is presumed here.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1973, 'temperature': 0.2})
